A||||5||BlackStang95||fiero question||||4||
Z||000000||BlackStang95||10-12-2001||12:47 AM||||This is two questions really, first one is with the sunroof secured in the front compartment...is it safe?  My friend seems to be afraid itll break during a hard turn or braking.  My other question is about the windshields.  the top of his 87 gt is an ugly yellow color...it looks like piss or something were all fieros like this? ||||reg||4
Z||000001||sqoach||10-12-2001||12:51 AM||||Glad to see you're wanting to know some info on Fieros.<BR>Yes, the sunroof is safe in the front. They wouldn't have made it like that if it were going to break. Just make sure the little foam pad things are there on the underside of the hood.<BR>All of them that I know of are tinted at the top of the windshield. Shouldn't be yellow though.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">            <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||10-12-2001||12:52 AM||||Um...with all my fiero expieriences Ive never heard either of these questions asked before....<BR>Yes the sunroof is safe in the front...Ive never heard of a problem with them breaking in "sharp turns" or whatever since 1984...Im sure the GM engineers know alittle more than your friend (thought probobly not much lol).<BR>I dont recall any "piss yellow" problems w/ the windshields anyway. Only thing I can think of is maybe your seeing the headliner throught the windshield (if its a tan int). It appears yellow from the outside..I noticed that on my Formula a while back to.||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||10-12-2001||02:03 AM||||The windshield glare tint on the top tends to fade over time. While it was originally a darker amber it has now faded over the years....the newer style windshields we replace have a darker green glare tint on the top.<P>For the sunroof glas there are two supports mounted to the forward side (in front of the spare tire) of the front compartment with 10mm bolts. These generally have either felt pads or rubber pads on them....on the rear of the front compartment you should have a mount which holds the sunroof wind deflector. This mount is held on with three 7mm screws. It covers the windshield wiper motor and the a/c redryer......<P>If any of these pieces are missing it is possible for the sunroof glass to shift in the front compartment.....otherwise, it is completely safe as that is where is was designed to be stored......I usually store the sunroof shield in the bag on top of the glass when I store it under the hood.....<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocks_sig.jpg">   </A><BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
